Here's the code for the function modp(g, n, p):
```
public int modp(int g, int n, int p) {
    // Compute g^n modulo p using exponentiation by squaring
    int result = 1;
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        result = (result * g) % p;
    }

    // Reduce the result to the range [1, p-1] if necessary
    while (result > p - 1) {
        result -= p;
    }

    return result;
}
```
