One way to address this issue is to use an interface or abstract class that defines the logging behavior, rather than a concrete logging framework. This way, you can implement the logging behavior using different logging frameworks, making the component more reusable.

Another approach is to use an IOC container, such as Unity or Spring.IOC containers allow you to manage dependencies and configure the components in your application. You can use an IOC container to manage the logging behavior and provide a common interface that can be used by different logging frameworks. This way, you can easily switch between logging frameworks without modifying your components.

