responses:
[{'model': 'codellama-13b-instruct', 'response': '  You can use the `CompletableFuture.handle` method to wrap the `Jedis` object in a `CloseableResource` object, which will automatically close the resource when the `CompletableFuture` is completed. Here's an example of how you can modify your code to do this:
```
@Override
public CompletableFuture<CloseableResource<Jedis>> execute() {
    if (!isServiceActive()) return CompletableFuture.completedFuture(null);
    return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> {
        try (Jedis jedis = pool.getResource()) {
            return new CloseableResource<>(jedis);
        } catch (RuntimeException e) {
            logger.severe("Impossibile ottenere una nuova risorsa Jedis!", e);
            throw new CompletionException(e);
        }
    }, executor);
}
```
The `CloseableResource` class is a custom class that you can define to wrap the `Jedis` object in a `Closeable` object. Here's an example of how you can define this class:
```
public class CloseableResource<T extends Closeable> implements Closeable {
    private final T resource;

    public CloseableResource(T resource) {
        this.resource = resource;
    }

    @Override
    public void close() throws IOException {
        resource.close();
    }
}
